{
 "name": "rope3_v9",
 "description": "Rope trolley v16: an inverted-U frame straddling the rope, hanging from two V-pulleys.\n\nTwo beam-brick side walls (y = +-16) hang from two driven V-pulleys riding on top of the rope (y = 0). Each\npulley is a pair of rubber-tyred wedge-belt wheels (4185 + 2815, r 15.2) 1.4 mm apart: the cord sits on both tyre\nedges, centred (no roll), and the tyres grip the cord. One XL motor (left wall) drives, through an 8T -> 24T main\nshaft in the channel and a 24T-24T-40T transfer row outboard right, both pulleys (1:5). The rear deck wheels\n(43 mm, under the rear pulley) are chain-driven 1:1 from the rear pulley axle; they push on the start deck and\nclimb the goal deck edge. The front deck wheels (30 mm) hover 6 mm above the deck line: the trolley starts with\nits front pulley already resting on the rope, and at the goal they only touch down once the front pulley has\nrolled off the end of the rope. A plate floor 6 mm above the rope joins the walls; heavy parts hang low (battery\nright, receiver left) so the trolley hangs like a pendulum under the rope.",
 "chassis": "wl_B8_a",
 "motor": "motor",
 "battery": "battery",
